Subject: notifications: hide a history group's oldest entries and keep its expander count true

The history collapses a notification group to its newest groupLimit
children. With expandUnread it also keeps every unread child newer than
lastRead, so a collapsed group hides an entry from its middle, and the
count it offers as "Show %1 More" is not the number it hides. The
history model turns expandUnread off, so a collapsed group shows its
newest two children and hides exactly the older ones.

"Show %1 More" is GroupChildrenCountRole less
ExpandedGroupChildrenCountRole, both read on the group's last visible
child, and each is re-announced to every child row of a group whenever
a row joins or leaves it:

- NotificationGroupingProxyModel reports the group's size on every
  child. When tryToGroup adds a row to a group it announces
  GroupChildrenCountRole on all of the group's children, and when a
  member is removed it announces it on all remaining children, the
  range taken from the group's own child count, not the number of
  top-level rows.
- NotificationGroupCollapsingProxyModel computes
  ExpandedGroupChildrenCountRole as its row count under the group, so
  it re-announces that role, with IsGroupExpandedRole, after a source
  row is inserted or removed and after a ReadRole change, which moves
  the expandUnread filter.

The history draws "Show %1 More" (and "Show Fewer") on a group's last
visible child, found by comparing ListView.section with nextSection. The
section is the desktop entry, which is empty for a sender that names none,
and nextSection is empty past the list's last row; a group of such a sender
at the bottom of the list, or followed by another one, never draws the
button, and its collapsed children cannot be reached. The row is taken as
the group's last when the next row is not inside a group or there is none,
which holds whatever the sections are.

The next row is read from the model, which QML does not track, so the
list keeps a revision that every layout change, move, insertion, removal
and reset bumps, and the binding reads it.

--- a/applets/notifications/FullRepresentation.qml
+++ b/applets/notifications/FullRepresentation.qml
@@ -270,6 +270,19 @@
             model: fullRepresentationRoot.appletInterface.expanded ? fullRepresentationRoot.historyModel : null
             currentIndex: -1
 
+            // Bumped whenever a row may have a different successor; a binding that reads the
+            // next row from the model reads this too, since the model call itself is not tracked.
+            property int rowOrderRevision: 0
+
+            Connections {
+                target: fullRepresentationRoot.historyModel
+                function onLayoutChanged() { list.rowOrderRevision++; }
+                function onRowsMoved() { list.rowOrderRevision++; }
+                function onRowsInserted() { list.rowOrderRevision++; }
+                function onRowsRemoved() { list.rowOrderRevision++; }
+                function onModelReset() { list.rowOrderRevision++; }
+            }
+
             topMargin: Kirigami.Units.largeSpacing
             bottomMargin: Kirigami.Units.largeSpacing
             spacing: Kirigami.Units.smallSpacing
@@ -406,6 +419,15 @@
                 required property int groupChildrenCount
                 required property int expandedGroupChildrenCount
 
+                // The expander belongs on the group's last visible row: the one followed by a
+                // top-level row or by none. Sections cannot tell, because a sender without a
+                // desktop entry has an empty section, the same as nextSection past the last row.
+                // It re-evaluates on list.rowOrderRevision, which every reordering bumps.
+                readonly property bool isLastInGroup: list.rowOrderRevision >= 0 && isInGroup
+                    && (index >= list.count - 1
+                        || !fullRepresentationRoot.historyModel.data(fullRepresentationRoot.historyModel.index(index + 1, 0),
+                                                                    NotificationManager.Notifications.IsInGroupRole))
+
                 // NOTE: The following animations replace the Transitions in the ListView
                 // because they don't work when the items change size during the animation
                 // (showing/hiding the show more/show less button) in that case they will
@@ -620,7 +642,7 @@
                                                             : i18nc("Expand to show n more notifications",
                                                                     "Show %1 More", (delegate.groupChildrenCount - delegate.expandedGroupChildrenCount))
                                 visible: (delegate.groupChildrenCount > delegate.expandedGroupChildrenCount || delegate.isGroupExpanded)
-                                    && delegate.ListView.nextSection !== delegate.ListView.section
+                                    && delegate.isLastInGroup
                                 onClicked: list.setGroupExpanded(delegate.index, !delegate.isGroupExpanded)
                             }
                         }
